{"id": "EUVD-2026-82102", "enisaUuid": "2d06f885-1da5-325d-a472-def99acaaf5b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npinctrl: mediatek: free EINT resources on unbind\n\nmtk_eint_do_init() creates an IRQ domain, populates it with a mapping for\nevery EINT line and installs a chained handler on the parent interrupt,\nbut none of these are ever released. This was harmless while the drivers\nwere built-in, but now that they can be built as modules and\nunbound/rmmod'd it leaves behind a dangling IRQ domain, interrupt mappings\nwhose chip data points at freed memory, and a chained handler that keeps\nfiring into that freed data.\n\nThe plain allocations in mtk_eint_do_init() already use the device-managed\ndevm_*() helpers, so tear the remaining resources down the same way:\nregister a devm action that detaches the chained handler, waits for any\nin-flight handler to finish, disposes of the per-line mappings and removes\nthe IRQ domain. This mirrors the device-managed lifecycle adopted for the\nGPIO chip and keeps the whole EINT setup self-cleaning on unbind.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:03:47", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/23252bc1cd9a58a039c9b1ae77b22d2b33da48e9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/903a7cdf63a81d3738594c5bd1b5955f58fda427", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/51552c8c60d3b1fecc062eab2d8cfeaa1cb339dd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7f6d898179ca4771ee602bdad4246c3952af83eb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e06785cba7f86d72abd531058b1a82d6952a7346", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/88292b7103d260e3e606eb3bb2794060a5fde48e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-fmh8-wm6j-9mrf", "CVE-2026-92481"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "14ea0ef6-6e78-39e8-88eb-f8eb69a31cb3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e46df235b4e605aa4e7609a27c118a1cccd4ff9a <51552c8c60d3b1fecc062eab2d8cfeaa1cb339dd"}, {"id": "203d34bd-c0e1-3eea-a9f2-2b31e9499622", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e46df235b4e605aa4e7609a27c118a1cccd4ff9a <23252bc1cd9a58a039c9b1ae77b22d2b33da48e9"}, {"id": "35819ff7-2015-38b3-bdc4-63446d768ebc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.18"}, {"id": "3b347ded-c885-3ba6-924e-acf63f60727a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "561aaf44-5d1e-3679-9899-a509ac4d3196", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "7cbf2767-a912-3e06-a3cc-de6a0158f25d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "aedeafd2-90c9-32f1-a845-2b3c8d6ad424", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e46df235b4e605aa4e7609a27c118a1cccd4ff9a <903a7cdf63a81d3738594c5bd1b5955f58fda427"}, {"id": "b2c73684-547e-3816-9e14-9c0b0b9ea420", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e46df235b4e605aa4e7609a27c118a1cccd4ff9a <7f6d898179ca4771ee602bdad4246c3952af83eb"}, {"id": "bd49e9fa-b37d-3d5f-80db-ad0bda920479", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e46df235b4e605aa4e7609a27c118a1cccd4ff9a <e06785cba7f86d72abd531058b1a82d6952a7346"}, {"id": "d8262723-f667-3997-9adf-1d34433c8fb9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e87841dc-6905-3c9e-8d4e-2834523a717f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "ee5a2171-f439-305e-84b0-3e305280e16a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "f7feff66-df7a-3883-afcf-132c48c64cc2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "f823b93b-aff0-3f9c-82b5-b047a470de6d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e46df235b4e605aa4e7609a27c118a1cccd4ff9a <88292b7103d260e3e606eb3bb2794060a5fde48e"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d946042d-0ea5-3497-b2e7-995eb72a5228", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}